# 3-device fallback — cloud vendor unavailable (spec §2.2).
# A tailscale/wireguard 家用 Linux host takes the slave-C role, labeled
# "降级 3 设备-noCloud 伪云" so downstream analysis knows this run has
# no true cross-internet tunnel path.

kind: topology
topology_enum: 3-device-nocloud
devices:
  - device_kind: laptop
    role: driver
    listen: 127.0.0.1:18092
  - device_kind: headless
    role: observer,slave-a
    listen: 127.0.0.1:18091
  - device_kind: windows
    role: slave-b
    listen: 127.0.0.1:18094
    fallback_label: "降级 3 设备-noCloud 伪云 (tailscale/wireguard 家用 Linux 顶 slave-C)"
workloads:
  - cross-device-code-mod
  - windows-only-artifact
per_workload_reps: 3
notes: |
  Dropped coverage: cross-internet tunnel (cloud sandbox). Tailscale/
  wireguard hop looks LAN-shaped, so this run does NOT measure
  agentserver real-tunnel round-trip cost — flag any
  TimeToCompletion consistency claim accordingly.
